{
  "_name": "t95_e2e_mutual_reqpubkey",
  "_desc": "Phase-1 Slice-2 MUTUAL reqpubkey gate (sealed-sender redesign §2). A WANT_PUBKEY H now APPENDS the requester's ed_pub[32], so ONE reqpubkey provisions BOTH directions in a single round — no QR, no second reqpubkey (the t94 flow needed two). Two seeded engine=meshroute FirmwareNodes with e2e_dm=true (SimController derives X25519+Ed25519 from each seed + set_crypto_identity); SAME seeds as t94 so alice's hash=0xf2e6f8d4, bob's hash=0x474f8542. Flow: (1) BEFORE the handshake alice's sealed `send bob` has no AUTHORITATIVE bob pubkey -> refuses (e2e_no_pubkey, never cleartext, no delivery). (2) alice `reqpubkey 474f8542` fires ONE HARD WANT_PUBKEY H carrying ALICE's pubkey -> bob (the owner) CACHES alice (peer_key_cached node:1) BEFORE answering TYPE-5 with bob's pubkey -> alice caches bob (peer_key_cached node:2). Both now hold both keys from the SINGLE exchange. (3) alice `send bob` seals AND bob trial-opens it -> delivered \"after-hs\" (enc=true push). (4) THE MUTUALITY PROOF: bob `send alice` seals using alice's key it cached during the handshake -- with NO bob-side reqpubkey -- and alice opens it -> delivered \"mutual-reply\". Idle + lossless (sigma_db=0) so the handshake is deterministic.",
